{
  "table": {
    "name": "products",
    "purpose": "Product/service catalog for a fleet fuel-card system (Czech-language data). Each row is one billable product or service item that can be charged to a fuel card: fuels and consumables (AdBlue), road-toll charges (Toll access-Austria, Toll DEU), fees (Servisn\u00ed poplatek, Acquirer Simple Fee), card issuance (Vyd\u00e1n\u00ed karty), groceries (Potraviny), vehicle parts (Katalyz\u00e1tor), and generic categories (Ostatn\u00ed zbo\u017e\u00ed = other goods, Ostatn\u00ed sl. = other services). The catalog is looked up from transactions_1k via ProductID. The 591 rows vs. max ID 630 means some IDs are unused (gaps in the numbering)."
  },
  "columns": {
    "Description": {
      "role": "free_text",
      "name": "Description",
      "description": "Human-readable name/label of the product or service, predominantly Czech with some English/German entries for tolls and fees. It is a label, not a key: 529 distinct values across 591 rows, so some names repeat (e.g. 'Ostatn\u00ed zbo\u017e\u00ed' = other goods, 'Servisn\u00ed poplatek' = service fee, 'Potraviny' = foodstuffs, 'Vyd\u00e1n\u00ed karty' = card issuance, 'V\u00fd\u00fa\u010dt.p.n\u00e1kl. stred.' \u2248 settlement of fuel costs per cost center). No units or codes beyond the literal text.",
      "status": "resolved"
    },
    "ProductID": {
      "role": "identifier",
      "name": "ProductID",
      "description": "Primary key: unique numeric identifier of a product/service item in the catalog (values 1\u2013630, 591 distinct, so some IDs are unused). It is the meaningful foreign-key target for transactions_1k.ProductID \u2014 each transaction line references the product purchased here. The additional statistical joins to transactions_1k.Amount and gasstations.ChainID are numeric coincidences (overlapping integer ranges), not semantic relationships.",
      "status": "resolved"
    }
  }
}
